      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FANTAXTIC (10) earns top billing after a fourth at this track in BM58+ grade where he had difficulty obtaining clear running. He rises in grade, but the weight relief and Carbery taking control from the apprentice hoop is a big push. Can bounce back to winning ways. SCREAM (6) is the major danger, coming back from Saturday company at Ascot after being tightened near the 250m, and his Bunbury NMW1Y win two starts ago reads well with Sharni Webster back on a horse she has won on three times. FIRE THE GUARD (9) has been holding his form, was third at Geraldton in BM58+ company and gets weight relief, although he also has to handle the grade rise. ORACLE SON (7) returns from a five-week freshening after a sound Geraldton fourth and a narrow win the run before, so he has genuine place claims if he transfers that form to this venue. FLICK THE SWITCH (3) can't be left out of calculations.",
